{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/941065-question-about-advanced-duration","id":941065,"title":"Question about Advanced Duration.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-31T23:28:50-07:00","id":941065,"title":"Question about Advanced Duration.","content":"In RAW, the rules for primary spell factor and Arcanum is the equation 1(default) plus x minus 1(Arcanum rating), but this only makes sense to me for standard duration. How does that help in deciding Advanced Duration for a spell? Or is the default going to still be just one hour until add penalties?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T23:46:19-07:00","id":941070,"title":"","content":"Both Standard and Advanced duration use the same mechanics. I am also not sure what it is you are asking and to me it sounds like you have gotten the mechanic wrong (but it might be the way you wrote it)<br /> <br /> Default is duration is 1 (easy enough).<br /> You then may increase it by Arcanum dots -1.<br /> Then you can increase it by adding penalties.<br /> <br /> So someone with 3 in an Arcanum can increase the duration by 2 extra steps without penalties. Standard 3 turns, and with Reach its one week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Memb